WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:06.410
So Donald Trump first got his worst polling
during this campaign so far down to Joe Biden

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:09.410
by 14 points nationally.

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:12.980
And these are just unconscionable numbers.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:18.310
And a report from Axios about what's going
on inside the Trump White House and inside

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:24.060
the Trump campaign shows panic, fear, anger
at what's going on.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:29.930
So this latest poll from CNN and CNN is rated
as a B plus pollster by 538.

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:32.180
Their polling is pretty good.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.130
They have Trump's approval down to 38 percent.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.300
That rivals the lows of Trump's presidency.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:42.970
And then in terms of Biden versus Trump for
November, this poll has Biden at 55.

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:44.300
Trump at forty one.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:49.489
Now, what's important about this poll, other
than Biden's absolutely ridiculous 14 point

00:00:49.489 --> 00:00:53.769
lead, is that Biden is well above 50 percent.

00:00:53.769 --> 00:01:01.179
If you look back to June of 2016, in other
words, this time in the 2016 election, Hillary

00:01:01.179 --> 00:01:03.739
Clinton was very rarely hitting 50 percent.

00:01:03.739 --> 00:01:06.230
You can go back and you can find a poll here
or there

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:09.290
where Hillary had 50, maybe 51.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:14.790
But in June of 2016, Hillary Clinton was mostly
polling in the low 40s and occasionally in

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:18.630
the high 40s with the occasional 50 or 51.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:25.940
Joe Biden is now regularly polling at 50 percent
or more in recent polls.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:31.680
And that is a very different starting point
than where Hillary Clinton was back in June

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:32.680
of 2016.

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:36.520
Now, the difference is Biden is running against
an incumbent, whereas Hillary Clinton running

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:40.840
against Trump was two challengers or two potential
candidates.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:45.640
And there is some degree to which one might
expect as we get closer to the election, people

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:50.160
will break for the incumbent, and that would
certainly benefit Donald Trump.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.950
So publicly, Trump is insisting that he's
doing really well.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:59.030
He very often will tweet versions of what
he tweeted this morning, this morning, saying,

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:02.240
quote, 96 percent approval rating in the Republican

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:03.240
Party.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:04.240
Thank you.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:10.149
The sources never cited the source is never
clear, but Trump posts that all the time.

00:02:10.149 --> 00:02:15.659
And publicly he's pretending that he's doing
really well and that Joe Biden can't win unless

00:02:15.659 --> 00:02:18.290
Democrats cheat in the fall or something like
that, which is hilarious.

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:22.700
By the way, privately, Donald Trump's aides
and advisers are coming to him and telling

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:26.620
him these polls don't look good and you need
to do something.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.590
They know how bad the polls are.

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:35.409
A source briefed on internal polls is calling
them, quote, brutal and seeing a major drop

00:02:35.409 --> 00:02:37.269
off in independent support.

00:02:37.269 --> 00:02:41.240
While Trump's Republican support is remaining
relatively high, his Democratic support is

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:42.900
extremely low.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.790
Independents have been shifting away from
Trump significantly in the last few months.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:53.510
The when the looting starts, the shooting
starts thing that Trump said is troubling

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:55.950
for some of Donald Trump's top aides.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:56.950
And

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:01.450
clearly, they know that Trump's disgustingly
divisive reaction to the protests have hurt

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:02.450
them.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:07.569
And they are saying Trump needs to instead
give a message of hope, optimism and unification.

00:03:07.569 --> 00:03:12.560
And from that recommendation came this idea
that's now being floated about maybe Trump

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:16.030
could give a, quote, major speech on race.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:21.609
Now, I have to tell you, as hilarious as a
major speech on race would be from Donald

00:03:21.609 --> 00:03:23.989
Trump, I don't even know that I would cover
it.

00:03:23.989 --> 00:03:29.040
Normally, I would stream major presidential
speeches, but I don't know that I would cover

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.040
that.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:32.010
It would be merely a propaganda piece.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:36.670
Trump probably would barely even understand
what he was reading off of his prompter.

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:39.959
It would be calculated to try to get a few
more points in a poll.

00:03:39.959 --> 00:03:43.150
And I don't even know that I would cover that
speech.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:44.930
Now a few insights into a Zoome

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:49.200
call that took place with Trump's top campaign
advisers, Corey Lewandowski.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.090
Ask the question, what is our message?

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:53.720
Which is a relevant question.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:56.950
It's not clear what Trump's message is right
now.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:02.489
They seem to settle on the idea of something
like a great American comeback theme.

00:04:02.489 --> 00:04:09.889
The idea of using those misreported jobs numbers
from last week to build this optimistic comeback

00:04:09.889 --> 00:04:14.700
strategy for the next five months, that's
going to be tough because Donald Trump, on

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:22.060
one hand, is appealing to his hardcore base
with his wild and hateful and divisive rhetoric,

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:25.400
talking about sending in the military ominous
weapons.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.580
That doesn't play well with a lot of people.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:32.889
But if Trump switches to a unification message
to try to get his polling up, it's not clear

00:04:32.889 --> 00:04:36.860
that that's going to play well with his hard
core supporters.

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:39.259
What would be nice would be for Trump to say,

00:04:39.259 --> 00:04:40.710
hey, you know what, guys?

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:41.770
We failed.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:42.840
We failed.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.120
The country has lost confidence in me.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.669
If they ever had it, we are all going to be
resigning.

00:04:48.669 --> 00:04:49.669
We failed.

00:04:49.669 --> 00:04:50.669
We are failures.

00:04:50.669 --> 00:04:51.669
And I'm sorry.

00:04:51.669 --> 00:04:52.669
That's what should happen.

00:04:52.669 --> 00:04:53.850
It will never happen.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:54.850
They are going to have.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:05:00.270
Be removed when you get a tick in, it attaches
to your body and you try to just pull it off.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:01.270
You can't.

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:03.389
The tick hangs on for dear life.

00:05:03.389 --> 00:05:05.770
They are going to have to be removed like
a deer tick.

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:08.129
You're going to have to pour alcohol on it.

00:05:08.129 --> 00:05:09.250
Take tweezers.

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:13.620
Squeeze it by the head and try to get it to
release its grip on your skin.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.730
That's the analogy of how they're going to
have to be removed.

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:19.850
These are some of Trump's best, worst numbers
ever.

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:22.690
But at the same time, 38 percent of the country

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:24.520
thinks he's doing a good job.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:25.659
That is horrifying.

00:05:25.659 --> 00:05:28.430
And it means he can win in November.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:32.889
And I don't know if the 38 percent are people
who are cultlike in their following of Trump

00:05:32.889 --> 00:05:36.819
or what he does doesn't matter or they're
not paying attention or they don't care or

00:05:36.819 --> 00:05:38.030
they're cognitively impaired.

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:39.990
I don't know what it is.

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:42.650
But he still has 38 percent support.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:44.020
He can still win.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:06:51.990
And we need to get out there and make sure
that we prevent the reelection in November.

